    <string name="about_support">This is a hobby and community project. Updates, device compatibility, fix times, and individual support are not guaranteed. Reproducible bug reports and contributions are welcome.</string>
    <string name="about_root">Core gestures do not require root. Akış Gesture works 100% rootless; root permission is only used for optional advanced actions (Custom su commands, instant screen lock).</string>
    <string name="about_root_title">🔑 Root Access — For Advanced Users Only</string>
    <string name="root_warning_title">⚠️ ROOT IS STRONGLY NOT RECOMMENDED!</string>
    <string name="root_warning_desc">Rooting compromises device security, voids warranty and service rights, and if done incorrectly can permanently brick your device. Regular users have absolutely no need to root their device and we strongly advise against it. This section exists solely as information for advanced users who already have a rooted device.</string>
    <string name="about_root_not_required_title">✅ Root is NOT Required!</string>
    <string name="about_root_not_required_desc">All core navigation gestures (Back, Home, Recents, Launch App, Media Controls, Screenshot, etc.) work 100% without root via standard Android Accessibility Service.</string>
    <string name="about_root_features_title">⚡ What Does Root Do In This App? (Optional)</string>
    <string name="about_root_features_desc">Root is used only for the optional foreground-app force-stop action and for rebinding the accessibility entry after an unexpected system drop. It is never required for core gestures and remains the responsibility of users who understand these system-level changes.</string>
<string name="about_root_privacy_desc" formatted="false">🛡️ Security &amp; Privacy: Even if root access is granted, Akış Gesture never transmits data over the internet. All your settings and rules stay 100% on your device.</string>

    <string name="about_upstream">Akış Gesture is based on the MIT-licensed OpenSwipe source code. OpenSwipe copyright and license notices are preserved; Akış Gesture is an independent project.</string>
